Input: {"question": "Which country is Yuriy Sarantsev a citizen of?", "source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 0, "end": 56, "text": "Title: The Red Curtain: Yuriy Sarantsev's Soviet Odyssey"}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 58, "end": 246, "text": "In the midst of the Soviet Union's golden age of cinema, a talented young actor named Yuriy Sarantsev emerged, captivating audiences with his charismatic performances on the silver screen."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 247, "end": 391, "text": "Born and raised within the Soviet borders, Sarantsev's life and career were inextricably linked to the nation that nurtured his artistic growth."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 392, "end": 506, "text": "The year was 1922, and the Soviet Union was still in its infancy, forged from the ashes of the Russian Revolution."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 507, "end": 646, "text": "As the newly formed government consolidated its power, the arts became an essential tool for promoting socialist ideals and national pride."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 647, "end": 801, "text": "It was against this backdrop that Sarantsev's journey began, his early years shaped by the Soviet system's emphasis on education and cultural development."}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 802, "end": 964, "text": "Growing up in a family of modest means, Sarantsev's parents encouraged his passion for the performing arts, enrolling him in local theater groups and drama clubs."}, "D1S8": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 965, "end": 1101, "text": "These formative experiences laid the foundation for his future success, as he honed his craft under the guidance of experienced mentors."}, "D1S9": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1102, "end": 1286, "text": "The Soviet Union's commitment to providing access to arts education for all citizens, regardless of social background, played a significant role in Sarantsev's development as an actor."}, "D1S10": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1287, "end": 1393, "text": "As Sarantsev's talent and reputation grew, he began to attract attention from prominent Soviet filmmakers."}, "D1S11": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1394, "end": 1542, "text": "His breakthrough role came in the late 1950s, when he starred in a critically acclaimed production of Mikhail Sholokhov's \"And Quiet Flows the Don.\""}, "D1S12": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1543, "end": 1714, "text": "This adaptation of the Nobel Prize-winning novel was a testament to the Soviet Union's rich literary heritage and its ability to produce world-class cinematic productions."}, "D1S13": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1715, "end": 1882, "text": "Sarantsev's subsequent filmography reads like a who's who of Soviet cinema, with collaborations with renowned directors such as Andrei Tarkovsky and Sergei Bondarchuk."}, "D1S14": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1883, "end": 2077, "text": "His performances in films like \"War and Peace\" (1966) and \"They Fought for Their Country\" (1975) cemented his status as a leading man of Soviet cinema, earning him numerous awards and accolades."}, "D1S15": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2078, "end": 2172, "text": "Throughout his career, Sarantsev remained deeply committed to the Soviet Union and its ideals."}, "D1S16": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2173, "end": 2310, "text": "He was an active member of the Soviet Actors' Union, using his platform to promote the values of socialism and international cooperation."}, "D1S17": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2311, "end": 2473, "text": "His involvement in various cultural exchange programs, including a notable tour of Eastern Europe and Cuba, further solidified his connection to the Soviet state."}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 0, "end": 136, "text": "As the fog rolled in off the Thames, Yuriy Sarantsev stepped out of the misty evening and into the warm glow of Simpson's-in-the-Strand."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 137, "end": 316, "text": "The venerable restaurant, a London institution since 1828, was a favorite haunt of his, and he had a particular fondness for their signature roast beef and a glass of fine claret."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 317, "end": 419, "text": "Tonight, however, he had a more pressing engagement – a meeting with his agent, the indefatigable Mrs."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 420, "end": 430, "text": "Pemberton."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 431, "end": 565, "text": "As he made his way to their usual table, Yuriy's eyes scanned the room, taking in the familiar sights and sounds of the establishment."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 566, "end": 725, "text": "The soft murmur of conversation, the clinking of glasses, and the occasional burst of laughter all blended together to create a sense of comfort and belonging."}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 726, "end": 844, "text": "It was a feeling he had grown accustomed to during his years in London, a city that had adopted him as one of its own."}, "D2S8": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 845, "end": 849, "text": "Mrs."}, "D2S9": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 850, "end": 949, "text": "Pemberton, resplendent in her emerald green hat and pearls, rose from her seat as Yuriy approached."}, "D2S10": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 950, "end": 1061, "text": "\"Darling Yuriy, you look every inch the leading man tonight,\" she exclaimed, her eyes sparkling with amusement."}, "D2S11": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1062, "end": 1191, "text": "\"I have some wonderful news – the Royal Shakespeare Company is interested in casting you as Hamlet in their upcoming production.\""}, "D2S12": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1192, "end": 1248, "text": "Yuriy's eyes lit up with excitement as he took his seat."}, "D2S13": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1249, "end": 1258, "text": "\"Ah, Mrs."}, "D2S14": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1259, "end": 1287, "text": "Pemberton, you are a marvel."}, "D2S15": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1288, "end": 1336, "text": "I would be honored to play the melancholy Dane.\""}, "D2S16": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1337, "end": 1534, "text": "As they delved into the details of the production, Yuriy's thoughts strayed to his early days in London, when he had first arrived as a young man with a dream of making it big on the British stage."}, "D2S17": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1535, "end": 1754, "text": "It had not been easy, of course – there had been struggles and setbacks aplenty – but he had persevered, driven by his passion for the craft and his determination to make a new life for himself in this adopted homeland."}, "D2S18": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1755, "end": 2022, "text": "And now, as he sat in Simpson's, surrounded by the trappings of British elegance and refinement, Yuriy felt a deep sense of pride and gratitude towards the United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland, the country that had taken him in and given him a chance to shine."}, "D2S19": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2023, "end": 2178, "text": "He was, in every sense of the word, a citizen of this great nation, and he knew that he would always be grateful for the opportunities it had afforded him."}}, "candidates": [{"candidate_id": "C0", "answer": "Soviet Union", "card_ids": ["d1:c0"]}, {"candidate_id": "C1", "answer": "United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland", "card_ids": ["d2:c0"]}], "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "d1", "card_id": "d1:c0", "entity": "Yuriy Sarantsev", "scope": "citizenship", "claim": "Yuriy Sarantsev is a citizen of the Soviet Union.", "answer": "Soviet Union", "quote": "Born and raised within the Soviet borders, Sarantsev's life and career were inextricably linked to the nation that nurtured his artistic growth.", "original_document_number": 1}, {"doc_id": "d2", "card_id": "d2:c0", "entity": "Yuriy Sarantsev", "scope": "citizenship", "claim": "Yuriy Sarantsev is a citizen of the United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland.", "answer": "United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland", "quote": "And now, as he sat in Simpson's, surrounded by the trappings of British elegance and refinement, Yuriy felt a deep sense of pride and gratitude towards the United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland, the country that had taken him in and given him a chance to shine. He was, in every sense of the word, a citizen of this great nation, and he knew that he would always be grateful for the opportunities it had afforded him.", "original_document_number": 2}], "initial_answers": ["Soviet Union", "United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland"]}
